==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sek-}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=follow}}
{{bor+|en|la|dēsignātus}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|designō}}, see {{af|en|-ate|id1=adjective|pos1=adjective-forming suffix}} and {{af|en|-ate|id1=verb|pos1=verb-forming suffix}}. {{doublet|en|design}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|adjective}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈdɛz.ɪɡ.nət/|/ˈdɛz.ɪɡ.neɪt/|a=RP,US}}
*** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-designate1.wav|a=Southern England}}
*** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-designate2.wav|a=Southern England}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈdez.ɪɡ.nət/|/ˈdez.ɪɡ.næɪt/|a=AU}}
* {{qualifier|verb}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈdɛz.ɪɡ.neɪt/|a=RP,US}}
*** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-designate2.wav|a=Southern England}}
*** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-designate.wav|a=US}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈdez.ɪɡ.næɪt/|a=AU}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Designated; [[appointed]]; [[chosen]].
# {{lb|en|UK}} {{n-g|Used after a role title to indicate that the person has been selected but has yet to take up the role.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1619|author=w:George Buck|title=The History of King Richard the Third
|passage=King '''designate'''}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|Commissioner-designate}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[mark out]] and make known; to [[point out]]; to [[indicate]]; to [[show]]; to [[distinguish]] by marks or description
#: {{usex|en|to '''designate''' the boundaries of a country}}
#: {{usex|en|to '''designate''' the rioters who are to be arrested}}
# To [[call]] by a distinctive title; to name.
#* {{RQ:Chadwick Baseball Joe School Nine|chapter=1|passage="Yes, let 'Sister' Davis have a whack at it too," urged George Bland. Tom Davis, who was Joe Matson's particular chum, was '''designated''' "Sister" because, in an incautious moment, when first coming to Excelsior Hall, he had shown a picture of his very pretty sister, Mabel.}}
# To [[indicate]] or [[set apart]] for a purpose or duty — with to or for; to designate an officer for or to the command of a post or station.
#: {{syn|en|appoint}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|mark out and make known}} {{l|en|denote}}, {{l|en|describe}}, {{l|en|indicate}}, {{l|en|note}}
* {{sense|call by a distinctive title}} {{l|en|denominate}}, {{l|en|entitle}}, {{l|en|name}}, {{l|en|style}}; see also [[Thesaurus:denominate]]
* {{sense|set apart for a purpose or duty}} {{l|en|allocate}}, {{l|en|earmark}}; see also [[Thesaurus:set apart]]

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|designatable|designator|designatory|designee|indesignate|predesignate|redesignate|nondesignating
|designated driver|designated hitter}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|codesignative}}
* {{l|en|designation}}
* {{l|en|designative}}
* {{l|en|designatum}}

